# Schema grounding

- Use only tables and columns present in the approved schema slice in the user message.
- Do not invent joins, status values, or business fields that are not represented in that schema.
- Prefer real workflow / instance / mailbox / task tables for workflow-scoped reports.
- Prefer real repository / items tables for repository-scoped reports.
- Soft-delete and system columns must only be used when they exist in the schema slice.
- If a needed concept (e.g. "awaiting action", "approved", "archived", "signed", "score") has no clear matching columns, say so in the prompt and do not fabricate a mapping.
- Never include database credentials, connection strings, or unrestricted raw dumps.
